<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The update feed Slate reads.

  The app asks for this one file and nothing else. Nothing about the person or
  their Mac is sent with the request. A build is only installed if the
  sparkle:edSignature below was made with the private key that matches
  SUPublicEDKey in Slate's Info.plist, so a swapped file cannot get in.

  To publish a release, see README.md, "Shipping a new version of the app".
  The signature comes from:

    "$SPARKLE_BIN/sign_update" dist/Slate-<version>.dmg
-->
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:sparkle="http://www.andymatuschak.org/xml-namespaces/sparkle">
  <channel>
    <title>Slate</title>
    <link>https://slatedictation.com/appcast.xml</link>
    <description>New versions of Slate.</description>
    <language>en</language>

    <item>
      <title>Version 1.1.3</title>
      <pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>6</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.1.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.4</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <ul>
          <li>When the talk key stops working, Slate now says so. The menu bar icon changes, and the menu tells you how to put it back.</li>
          <li>Putting it back has a step that is easy to miss, so Slate spells it out: if Slate is already in the Accessibility list, take it out and add it again.</li>
          <li>The welcome card no longer sits against the camera notch.</li>
        </ul>
      ]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://slatedictation.com/Slate-1.1.3.dmg"
                 length="7880328"
                 type="application/octet-stream"
                 sparkle:edSignature="h75R+J/fXl4IgJkJGOPHldaKxj9c+6tVdpq2jdSWcvotYP/vrfj6UbpuG97696Kz0DA7vHi5nTu/Pl5rnaG0DQ==" />
      <!-- Signed against the notarized, stapled DMG (3 Aug 2026), and checked
           with sign_update in verify mode against this exact file before
           pushing. Both the signature and the byte length change every time
           the DMG is rebuilt, so re-run sign_update and update both together.
           For whoever edits this next: an XML comment may not contain a
           double hyphen, so spell command flags out as words in here. -->
    </item>

    <item>
      <title>Version 1.1.2</title>
      <pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 03:20:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>5</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.1.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.4</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <ul>
          <li>Changing headphones mid sentence no longer cuts your words short. Slate waits for the new microphone and keeps going.</li>
          <li>If the microphone does go away for good, Slate types what it heard instead of leaving the pill on screen.</li>
          <li>Quitting Slate while your music is paused now starts the music again.</li>
        </ul>
      ]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://slatedictation.com/Slate-1.1.2.dmg"
